.env
# Any .env variant is a credentials file — the plain `.env` rule alone does not
# match `.env.aura`, `.env.production` and friends, which is how a secret gets
# committed by accident. The example template is negated back in because it
# contains no values.
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
data/papers.db
qdrant_storage/

# Runtime extraction failure log
data/failed_extractions.log
uv.lock

# setuptools build artifacts (produced now that the editable build works)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
data/rejected_extractions.jsonl
